abstract = {Welcome to CHIWORK'26, the 5th Annual Symposium on Human-Computer Interaction for Work held at the Ars Electronica Center in Linz, Austria.CHIWORK is the annual symposium that aims to grow our understanding of how Human-Computer Interaction (HCI) will support work in the future. Advances in computing technologies continue to transform how we work, collaborate, learn, and organize. Human-computer interaction (HCI) plays a central role in shaping these transformations by examining how technologies can support meaningful, sustainable, and inclusive futures of work. As emerging systems such as AI agents, automation, data-driven infrastructures, and novel collaborative environments increasingly become a reality in workplaces, HCI research helps us understand not only how work becomes more efficient but also how it becomes engaging and fulfilling.},
